{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>The troubles of my heart</b> — This is the understanding planted in the heart; therefore it is called by its name. <b>Make wide</b> is an intransitive verb. The meaning: that they are many. Some say: <b>my heart</b> is the object and it is distant, for after it comes <b>out of my distresses</b>."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:33.477518176Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}